// The module search path: `--lib` directories, searched in order.
//
// `import foo` looks for foo/module.ae or foo.ae in each directory of the
// search path, left to right, and the first one found wins; every import
// walks the path on its own. `--lib dir` adds a directory, and repeating
// it, or giving one value with the platform's separator (`--lib
// "lib:vendor"`, `;` on Windows), adds several; AETHER_LIB_DIR holds the
// same list. With none, the path is lib/. Here foo is in both lib/ and
// vendor/, so the order decides which one this program gets, and bar,
// only in vendor/, is found there either way. Swap the two `--lib`s and
// foo comes from vendor/. `ae lib-path --lib a --lib b` prints the path a
// build will search.
//
// Run: ae run examples/06-tooling/04-lib-path/main.ae --lib examples/06-tooling/04-lib-path/lib --lib examples/06-tooling/04-lib-path/vendor
// See: docs/module-system-design.md

import foo
import bar

main() {
    println("foo says: ${foo.origin()}")
    println("bar says: ${bar.origin()}")
}

// Output:
// foo says: lib/, the project's own copy
// bar says: vendor/, the only copy
